{"skill":{"slug":"excalidraw","displayName":"Excalidraw Diagram Generator"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769889062452,"changelog":"Initial release: hand-drawn style diagrams from Excalidraw JSON with auto-binding arrows, roughjs rendering, Virgil/Cascadia fonts","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5106,"sha256":"01ac5f59b87949f36076bb74da8492125677d860aedde3f4fc7951f73c9ec35a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/element-schema.md","size":3103,"sha256":"b50b77521a47ead922125285532d7e46eaf2cb753699a235375c71206bd42c99","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/package-lock.json","size":35739,"sha256":"8985b035ad87065e91f9d1fd3c58e4395ff8dbb5636d4f9c0555e7f3d7b488d8","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/package.json","size":201,"sha256":"bba6711557208418126a2f45294d7a14e254bd132052697228b494ff3f00b93b","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/render.js","size":21259,"sha256":"d9c1251c4a75f2c7170f3479b6515f6041d4d6cd55c2433d7a81062fd0138867","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/setup.sh","size":2133,"sha256":"4ccea81e7484662403785bc9305ee4e1106ccd45e7ca18a6f29fcbb97b22b48f","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2083,"sha256":"ac790e2964624c5281ce5bbac9d0c37e83338ce242e921dd2da26a8d61736baf","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789025285729,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f5ad021820a5d26f768ea1e3ec929e50c8a9abda60ef14c8be3edf889ad6b45c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f5ad021820a5d26f768ea1e3ec929e50c8a9abda60ef14c8be3edf889ad6b45c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: excalidraw\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill's functionality is to generate Excalidraw diagrams from JSON input and render them as PNG images. The `SKILL.md` provides clear instructions for the AI agent to generate JSON, save it to `/tmp`, and then execute a local `node` script (`scripts/render.js`) to produce a PNG, also in `/tmp`. The `scripts/setup.sh` installs necessary Node.js dependencies and downloads fonts (Virgil from `cdn.jsdelivr.net` and Cascadia Code from `github.com/microsoft`) required for rendering. The `scripts/render.js` processes local files and does not initiate any external network requests. All actions are directly aligned with the stated purpose, use standard temporary file locations, and download from legitimate sources, showing no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, or prompt injection.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160522571},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":67,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789025285729},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill appears intended to render Excalidraw diagrams, but its setup process has supply-chain and temporary-file safety issues that should be reviewed before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Node, filesystem access, and local rendering libraries are proportionate for PNG generation. Network access during setup is related to font installation, but vendored or hash-verified assets would be safer.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"setup.sh runs npm install and downloads third-party font assets over HTTPS without pinned hashes or signature checks, then parses/extracts them. package-lock.json also contains scanner-reported vulnerable transitive dependencies.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are narrow but use predictable /tmp filenames and a shell command without explicit validation or permission boundaries. This is purpose-aligned for rendering but under-scoped for safer multi-user or untrusted-input environments.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The setup persists npm dependencies/fonts under the skill scripts directory and chmods render.js; it does not install services, scheduled tasks, shell profile changes, or elevated-privilege persistence. Fixed /tmp paths in setup remain a local race/symlink concern.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The core purpose is coherent: SKILL.md instructs the agent to create Excalidraw JSON, run a local Node renderer, and send back a PNG. The renderer reads JSON/stdin and writes a PNG, with no evidence of credential access, data exfiltration, persistence hooks, or unrelated behavior.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable running a local Node-based renderer with setup-time network downloads. Run setup as an unprivileged user, avoid sudo, prefer npm ci from the lockfile, update the vulnerable transitive dependencies, and use unique temporary input/output paths rather than predictable /tmp names when rendering content influenced by others.","findings":"[SC4] unexpected: Accepted as a real supply-chain concern: package-lock.json includes form-data 4.0.5 as a jsdom transitive dependency. The artifact does not show multipart upload handling, so exploitability appears indirect, but the vulnerable pinned dependency should be updated.\n[SC4] unexpected: Accepted as a real supply-chain concern: package-lock.json includes ws 8.19.0 via jsdom. The renderer appears offline and does not create WebSocket connections, reducing direct exposure, but the vulnerable dependency remains unnecessary risk.\n[LP3] expected: The local node render command is expected for this skill's purpose. The concern is downgraded to scoping guidance because there is no evidence of hidden shell behavior or unrelated command execution.\n[SQP-2] expected: Writing input and output files for rendering is expected, but the documented /tmp/<name> pattern is predictable and lacks validation guidance, so users should use unique temporary paths for untrusted or shared environments.\n[E1] expected: Overridden as data exfiltration: the cited curl command downloads a font asset and does not upload user data. It remains relevant as an unverified external download risk.\n[SC1] expected: The npm dependencies are expected for rendering. The package.json semver ranges are partially mitigated by package-lock integrity entries, but exact pins or npm ci would improve reproducibility.\n[T08] expected: Accepted as an install-time supply-chain concern: setup.sh downloads versioned font assets from jsDelivr and Microsoft GitHub without independent integrity verification before parsing or use.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a local safety concern: setup.sh uses fixed shared paths /tmp/cascadia.zip and /tmp/cascadia_extract, which can allow local race, symlink, or cross-process interference on multi-user systems.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789025285729}}}}}